    "text": "Walter Duranty got a Pulitzer Prize for pushing Soviet propaganda as truth. He denied that there was a famine in progress in the USSR, a famine that was the result of the government's own actions. Duranty's reporting was a key factor in FDR granting diplomatic recognition to the USSR.\nAt a dinner at the Waldorf-Astoria in November 1933, where Soviet Foreign Minister Litvinov was in attendance, the names of the guests were named, and each received polite applause - except for Walter Duranty. In his case it was prolonged applause and cheers. The attendees knew that it was Duranty that had made the event possible.",
